  "name": "@brainstrike/agent",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "//@ai-sdk/openai": "PINNED EXACTLY, and deliberately behind latest. 4.0.50 stopped preserving a tool-result own providerMetadata.openai.itemId and emits the CALL id for both item_reference entries, re-regressing the fix from 4.0.18 (changeset bc43dc2). That defeats OpenAIToolSearchHistoryCompat: duplicate item_references reach OpenAI, which rejects them. Bisected against the real SDK by src/__tests__/openai-tool-search-history-compat.spec.ts — 4.0.43/4.0.46/4.0.47/4.0.49 pass, 4.0.50/4.0.55/4.0.59/4.0.60 fail. REVIEW TRIGGER: re-run that spec whenever a dependency-bump PR proposes raising this, and raise it the moment the spec goes green on a newer version. It IS a CI gate, not a manual step \u2014 packages/agent/vitest.config includes src/**/__tests__/*.spec.ts, so a bump to a regressed version fails the Unit lane rather than merging green. Cost, stated: @ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock depends on a newer openai directly, so the tree carries a second copy — packages/agent resolves 4.0.49 (asserted against the installed manifest), and Bedrock OpenAI-compatible models do not use the Responses-API item_reference path this compensates for. The openai mirror contract resolves the SAME copy on purpose \u2014 createRequire from packages/agent/package.json \u2014 so the nested Bedrock copy cannot become the version it reads.",
